<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<div>
  Replaces <strong>existing</strong> scalar values in JSON and .NET XML configuration files
  (<code>appsettings.json</code> and <code>web.config</code>) from a Pipeline step, preserving every
  byte it was not asked to change: comments, indentation, key order, attribute order, quote style,
  BOM state and line endings all survive.
  <p>
    Values may be literals or Jenkins Secret Text credentials. Nothing is ever created: a property
    path that does not resolve is a missing path, never a new field.
  </p>
</div>
